<title>SPAIN: Spain had Feb c/a surplus 128.7 bln pta.</title>
<headline>Spain had Feb c/a surplus 128.7 bln pta.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		FEB 97   JAN  97     FEB 96</p>
<p>  C/A balance			 128.7     168.8	 1.8</p>
<p>  Trade balance		    -190.2     -61.3    -188.9</p>
<p>  Services			    153.6     154.6     115.1</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts	    190.1     195.2     153.5</p>
<p>  Other services		    -36.5     -41.1     -38.4</p>
<p>  Dividend income		   -26.0     -63.3	-1.3</p>
<p>  Transfers			   191.2     139.4	76.9</p>
<p>  BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		FEB 97   JAN  97     FEB 96</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		     23.3     62.3	  5.0</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		  -32.9   - 26.3     -164.1</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad     -107.0   -313.9     -326.4</p>
<p>  Foreign investment in Spain   -414.9   -220.3     -812.1</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,deposits abroad  692.2   -191.4	583.0</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain   113.6   1220.3	352.8</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves	    -316.7   -521.0	 38.6</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional. Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is positive for 30.4 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
